---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import {
  MILESTONES,
  STATUS,
  capabilitiesForMilestone,
} from "../lib/capabilities.mjs";
---

<Page
  title="Roadmap — Shared Auth"
  description="The shared-auth parity roadmap: five milestones from routing the identity code that already exists to shipping embeddable components and a self-serve enterprise portal."
  eyebrow="Parity roadmap"
  heading="Five milestones from identity plane to identity product."
  lede="The authentication core is deep. The product surface around it is not. These milestones close that distance in the order that a buyer notices."
>
  {
    MILESTONES.map((milestone) => {
      const items = capabilitiesForMilestone(milestone.id);
      return (
        <section id={milestone.id}>
          <h2>{milestone.name}</h2>
          <p class="lede">{milestone.goal}</p>
          <div class="table-wrap">
            <table>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Capability</th>
                  <th>Status</th>
                  <th>Area</th>
                  <th>Scope</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                {items.map((capability) => (
                  <tr>
                    <td>
                      <a href={`/features/#${capability.id}`}>
                        {capability.title}
                      </a>
                    </td>
                    <td>
                      <span
                        class={`status ${STATUS[capability.status].className}`}
                      >
                        {STATUS[capability.status].label}
                      </span>
                    </td>
                    <td>{capability.categoryName}</td>
                    <td>{capability.note}</td>
                  </tr>
                ))}
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </section>
      );
    })
  }
  <section id="principles">
    <h2>What we will not build</h2>
    <div class="grid-3">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>A configurable flow engine</h3>
        <p>
          An arbitrary authenticator graph is an enormous surface with a small
          audience. Ceremonies stay typed and fixed so their guarantees stay
          provable.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Push-notification MFA</h3>
        <p>
          It requires a first-party authenticator app and a push fleet. Passkeys
          reach the same assurance with less operational surface.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Outbound provisioning and access reviews</h3>
        <p>
          Pushing accounts into downstream applications and running
          certification campaigns is identity governance — a different product.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="cta-row">
    <a class="primary" href="/features/">Full capability register →</a><a
      href="https://github.com/shared-auth">Follow the work on GitHub ↗</a
    >
  </div>
</Page>
